From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bytecoin Community <community@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] walletd for the browser (WebAssembly)

The source already has __EMSCRIPTEN__ paths for walletd (requests from
JavaScript through embind, fetch() to the node, wallet and cache in
IndexedDB, ext_create_wallet / ext_open_wallet RPC), used by the 2019
Bytecoin Zero web wallet, but no entry point and no build for them.

- src/main_wasm.cpp: entry point, the equivalent of `walletd --app`.
  Exports create_mnemonic() and check_mnemonic() to JavaScript, because
  walletd has no RPC for a new mnemonic. Commits the wallet cache every
  15 s instead of 111 s, since a browser tab can close at any moment.
- Wallet file encryption (WalletNodeExt): with a non-empty wallet_password
  the IndexedDB wallet file, which holds the mnemonic, is stored as
  "bcnwallet2" | salt | iv | ChaCha20 | HMAC-SHA256, keys from
  PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA512 (250000 iterations). The MAC also covers the
  IndexedDB key, so a file copied into another wallet's slot does not
  open. "bcnwallet1" files (100000 iterations, no key in the MAC) and
  plain files from older builds open as before and are rewritten as
  "bcnwallet2" on first open with a password. ext_set_password
  re-encrypts. Wrong password gives error 207.
- WalletSync: a node that refuses sync_mem_pool with "Authorization
  Required" (the public node01/node02.bytecoin.org do) is no longer a
  sync error repeated every few seconds. walletd stops asking for the
  memory pool and keeps syncing blocks; unconfirmed incoming transfers
  then appear once they are in a block.
- WalletHDJson::export_keys() returns the mnemonic (was a TODO returning
  an empty string), so get_wallet_info with need_secrets can back it up.
- MulticoreWallet: the worker variant (-Dbytecoin_WASM_WORKERS, default in
  wasm-wallet/emcc_build.sh) no longer creates nested workers, which some
  browsers lack. walletd posts work to the page, the page runs one
  walletworker per CPU core and returns results via walletd_pool_result().
  The worker count comes from navigator.hardwareConcurrency (2..8).
  Without the define, a single-threaded variant prepares outputs on the
  walletd thread in ~50 ms slices.

Build with Emscripten 3.1.64 (see wasm-wallet/emcc_build.sh). Node-side
files (Node*, BlockChain*, Archive, Ledger, Trezor, http/Client) do not
compile for WebAssembly and are not needed. Consensus and native builds
unchanged.
